MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_001: They turned out great. This ought to be good.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_002: Cai. Planning to eat all that fish yourself?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_003: Oh, hey, Bertrand. I was thinking I'd share some with\npeople in the village nearby.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_004: When this type of fish is dried out, it keeps for\nmonths. And you can eat it as is. Pretty handy.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_005: I'm sure they'll be grateful. It must have been a lot\nof work, catching and drying so many fish.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_006: Yeah, but I've got a knack for it.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_007: These wildflowers here taste great if you boil them.\nMaybe you want to try some with me later?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_008: Sure. You're quite resourceful, aren't you?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_009: If you were left in the wilderness alone, I imagine\nyou'd have no trouble getting back.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_010: Well, I did grow up in the mountains. And then\nthere's the fact that Pop trained me.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_011: Ah, yes, Castor.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_012: He'd send me running through the forest for days, or\nhe'd make me swim upstream nonstop, stuff like that.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_013: He was pretty tough on me. There were times when\nI was like, "I hate you so much right now, Pop!"
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_014: Well, that is a grueling regimen. I don't think military\ntraining is so rigorous.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_015: Thanks to that training, I'm confident that no one's\ngonna take me down easily.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_016: I suppose that's just what Castor was hoping for.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_017: Hm?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_018: He gave you the knowledge and skills to make it on\nyour own, even if he wasn't there.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_019: Hehe... I'm not sure the old man put such deep\nthought into it.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_020: But that's what I mean. Pop's training is the reason\nI've survived so far in this war-torn world.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_021: What a gift that is. After all, you can't accomplish\nanything with your life if you lose it.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_022: I only had a little time with Castor, but I could tell\nhe cared deeply about you.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_023: Looking back, his training was meaningful, and\nkinda fun sometimes too.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_024: It was just me and him, talking, laughing, sparring,\nenjoying a meal.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_025: Cai?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_026: Bertrand, I know you're busy.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_027: But maybe you could visit Pop's grave and leave\nsome flowers sometime. I'm sure he'd appreciate it.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_B_028: Of course. I'll plan on it.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_001: Bertrand, thank you for taking time to visit\nPop's grave.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_002: Think nothing of it. I was glad I could tell him what\na fine young man you've grown into.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_003: I'm sure he'd be proud seeing how strong and\nimpressive his son is today.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_004: Hehe... I hope so.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_005: Nothing makes a parent happier than seeing their\nchild grow up well.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_006: Then your parents must be really proud. Their son's\nbecome a great king.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_007: I bet you were surprised by all that yourself.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_008: I was. I wish I could have told my family about it...\nThey were killed before I took the throne.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_009: Ah! I-I'm sorry!
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_010: No need to apologize. You didn't know.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_011: My focus now is building a nation where no one has\nto feel the sadness I did.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_012: Where whole families can't be killed at the whim of\none person in power.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_013: That sounds like you. You don't want your suffering\nto happen again, to anyone.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_014: And you know I'm always here to help with that.\nJust say the word. Anything you need.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_015: Well, not "anything." Castor wouldn't want me to put\nyou in danger.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_016: Don't worry about me. Remember when I said no\none's gonna take me down easily?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_017: Anyway, Pop would want me to make myself useful\nto you.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_018: I'd argue, but I doubt you'd much listen. And in truth,\nit's a welcome offer.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_019: I accept your help, Cai Castor.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_020: I'm in. Together we'll build this new world you're\ntalking about.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_021: Yes—for our peoples now, and for the generations\nto come.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_022: Hm. Actually, on that note.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_023: If I had a son, I think I'd like to give him your\nfather's name.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_024: Your son would be...the prince of Brezarant,\nwouldn't he?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_025: Right. What better model for a prince than Castor's\ncaring nature?
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_026: I'm so proud to have known him—to know his son.\nI-it's just a thought.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_027: I think it's a great idea. Prince Pop is a good name.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_028: I'm kidding. When Prince Castor is ready, I'll be\naround to train him good and proper.
MID_SE_Kai_Bel_A_029: I should hope so. I'd like for him to turn out as well\nas you have.